{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1377389-unchained-in-manch-vegas-session-2-3-and-4-recap","id":1377389,"title":"Unchained in Manch-Vegas: Session 2, 3, and 4 Recap","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-30T13:01:51-07:00","id":1377389,"title":"Unchained in Manch-Vegas: Session 2, 3, and 4 Recap","content":"So my DtD game picked up more steam with the coronavirus situation. Online weekly games definitely help bring people together at this time.<br /> <br /> The 2nd session wasn't as well planned out as I wanted it to be. And when it came to our last session (4) I realized I needed to re-calibrate the story from a &quot;Investigate this New Problem&quot; to a more community centered investigation. Where the players set their sights on problems and so they have more time to gather resources and work on their covers, which I'll delve more in session 5 if I can.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Session 2: The Investigation</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Liberty Griswald left to meet Alan Thorne at the Crossroads tavern. Alan couldn\u2019t make it, but sent word ahead to a friend of his Molly. The two are able to identify that all three sleeper agents who attacked Alan\u2019s boss attended the same philosophy class. Molly goes undercover as an auditor for the philosophy class, but Prof. Draco is paranoid enough to think that Molly is onto him.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Draco calls class early and runs to a nearby Dunkin\u2019 Donuts. As soon as Liberty and Molly arrive they can see the gears of the God-Machine all over the Dunkin\u2019 Donuts. The Infrastructure\u2019s purpose is unknown to them. Inside there is a Simulacra operating the counter and Stigmatic worker. Liberty is able to ease drop a little bit before the Stigmatic recognizes him as an interloper. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Griswald pulls out his pistol and Merciless Gunmans the Simulacra and Stigmatic. Prof. Draco falls to the floor as Molly and Liberty grab him for interrogation.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Session 3: The Jenga Tower</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Molly opens up a doorway to her bolthole (easy access) and chucks Prof Draco into it. Inside they managed to get a better idea of what happened. Prof Draco was brought on as an ethics consultant onto a \u201cgovernment subliminal training\u201d project. He believed the students they were turning into Sleeper Agents were CIA operatives. The reason he sent them to kill Alan\u2019s boss was because he found out that his wife was having an affair with him. They also discover that two other professors were part of the project.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Molly and Liberty think he thinks he\u2019s telling the truth, but Molly decides to download his memory of the last hour and modify his memory (Memory Theft). In her download she finds out that Prof Draco confessed his misuse of the Sleeper Agents to the Stigmatic who responded \u201cIt was all part of God\u2019s plan.\u201d Hinting that the God-Machine expected the Prof to be the fall guy for this. Molly modifies Draco\u2019s memory to believe he shot the Simulacra and Stigmatic as part of an exchange about a wrong order. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Liberty and Molly pretended to be a father and daughter visiting the SNHU campus. With the campus on lockdown due to the shooting they managed to get in contact with the psych professor who worked with Prof Draco, Prof Roberts. They figure out that she got a piece of infrastructure from an Angel that works in tandem with a drug. After taking part in Roberts's study she admits that there are at least 30 sleeper agents among the student population.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Molly pockes one of the drugs and takes it to a crime lab technician friend of hers, Chelsey. Chelsey is able to identify the drug as a new street drug that\u2019s been making its way through the homeless population. The main effect being homeless people developing fugue personalities for a short time. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Molly and Griswald manage to track a man in a business suit passing out \u201cfree samples\u201d. It takes them seconds to identify this guy as a Reptilian. Griswald manages to knock out the Reptilian and Molly does Mind Reading. She manages to uncover that the Reptilians are working out of a Burger King, but are working for an Angel in a Hawaiian T-Shirt and Sunglasses.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Session 4: Start of Rebellion</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Molly, Griswald and Alan get an email from another Demon, Zechariah. They meet up at an AA meeting held at the Manchester Public Library. Though there are only three other individuals. Mr Black (A tattoo\u2019d punk rocker), Mrs. White (An Lawyer), and Sudo (A Bookish Hacker).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Zechariah presented a report on how their Free Agency of individuals looking out for one another has lost contact with Boston based Agencies. The only conclusion is that the God-Machine has won Boston and set its eyes on New Hampshire. All of the Demons are reporting an increase in Angel activity. Mrs. White brings up the idea that the Free Agency needs to aim their sights on fighting the God-Machine. Whereas Mr. Black proposes building an arsenal of souls and gadgets. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A vote is held and nearly unanimously Mrs. White is nominated as leader of the new Insurgent Agency. Mr. Black decided to take his leave to start his own Temporal Agency. Mrs. White lets him go and tells the newly minted agency to look for Infrastructure and disrupt the system.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alan decides the best course of action is to set up a shell company in a mill building to act as a front for their Demonic mission, Reasoning Incorporated. Griswald and Molly decide to dismantle the Dunkin\u2019 Donuts infrastructure. In the closed Dunkin\u2019 Donuts they figure out that throwing non-donuts into the frier is the lynchpin. Keeping a safe distance they watch as the Dunkin\u2019 reverts to a gas station and two mysterious Men in Black appear, government agents under the instruction of the God-Machine. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Griswald uses his In My Pocket ability to produce a small tracking device. The device is similar to one of those lost key devices, but they manage to hide it on the Men in Black\u2019s car. Now they\u2019ll have a warning if the Men in Black get too close. With the help of Alan they are able to use the tracker to locate where the Men in Black\u2019s HQ is. Their new plan is to infiltrate their facility and take down the Infrastructure that is supporting them. But they need to up their arsenal to pull off such a feat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}